# Liquid Glass look — notes for our theme

What makes the new macOS look feel like glass:
- translucent material with strong background blur (`backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(180%)`);
- a bright specular edge on top and a subtle inner shadow at the bottom;
- content underneath tints the material, so the same panel looks different over different wallpapers;
- rounded continuous corners (squircle-ish) and generous padding;
- motion: panels morph rather than just fade; springs, not linear easing.

Our identity: violet accent (#5E5CE6 dark, #5856D6 light), atom logo glowing softly on the boot screen.

Performance: blur is expensive. Limit the number of stacked blurred layers, and provide a "reduce transparency" setting that swaps glass for solid surfaces. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
